    schema:about "Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A finite-element or measured growth field; 3D mechanical blade expansion; polar PIN1 dynamics on a growing domain",
        "does_not_claim: Loop closure / areole formation or quaternary areole subdivision (beta_1 = 0 in every solved configuration; the specimen has 1843 areoles)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated segmentation of the SHA-256-pinned cleared dicot leaf (primary midrib, secondary angle 52.93 +- 2.53 deg, 1843 closed areoles, vein areal coverage 0.416)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: PRESCRIBED (Pass 2, retained and now labelled): 2-pathway exponent sweep p in {0.5, 1.0, 1.4, 2.0, 2.5} (the p = 1.4 point uses a special-cased eff_beta = 0.1766), analytic 12-column and 18x14 D/S profiles with hard-coded dip ratios (0.3105 / 0.6895), a Gaussian Sachs bypass centreline with constants 0.9852 / 0.0804, and two hand-drawn Feugier venation graphs (V=16/E=15 -> beta_1 = 0; V=28/E=41 -> beta_1 = 14)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: SOLVED (Pass 3): Mitchison (1980) facilitated-diffusion canalization with soft-saturating feedback alpha |phi|^2/(1+phi^2/phi_s^2) on a hexagonal cell lattice that divides 12x11 -> 24x22 -> 48x44 (75 -> 312 -> 1281 cells) with conductance inheritance; vein cells 7 -> 29 -> 155, nesting of new strands inside pre-existing panels 0.81 / 0.77, S_vein/S_par = 0.67 (emergent), sink intake / production 0.98, beta_1 = 0 at every stage (also 0 with the irreversible-differentiation ablation)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: SOLVED (Pass 3): Sachs (1981) transverse incision on a 20x16 hex stem with a pre-established strand: sink intake 0.991 (incised, canalizing) vs 0.609 (alpha = 0 NPA control) vs 0.988 (intact), 6-cell lateral deflection; hop-count path ratio L_wounded/L_intact = 1.00 (metric insensitive to lateral deflection)",
        "reported_in_source: Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375: PIN1 carrier-allocation dynamics, open trees vs closed areoles; Feugier & Iwasa (2006) 243:235-244: canalization alone does not close loops",
        "reported_in_source: Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109: facilitated-diffusion canalization dD_ij/dt = alpha |phi_ij|^p + beta - gamma D_ij with phi_ij = D_ij (S_i - S_j); linear feedback gives diffuse flow, quadratic feedback gives winner-take-all 1-cell strands whose auxin concentration drops below the parenchyma (S_vein < S_par)",
        "reported_in_source: Mitchison (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 295:461-471 & Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262: polar auxin transport canalization and C-shaped vascular bypass regeneration around a transverse stem incision",
        "reported_in_source: Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev. 20:1015-1027 & Kang & Dengler (2004) Int. J. Plant Sci. 165:231-242: higher-order veins form progressively inside areoles bounded by lower-order veins",
        "transfer_boundary: Facilitated diffusion (Mitchison 1980) is solved; polar PIN1 carrier allocation (Mitchison 1981 / Feugier 2005) is only verified algebraically (Law 3) and the hand-drawn graphs are not its output",
        "transfer_boundary: Hexagonal cellular lattice with isotropic 2x refinement stands in for a growing leaf blade; strand orientations are quantised to ~30/60/90 deg so the branch-angle comparison with the specimen (52.9 deg) is lattice-limited",
        "transfer_boundary: Reference values 1.38 / 0.985 / 0.08 (Sachs) and the exponent-regime table in the pinned reference JSON are not digitised from any figure; they are carried as qualitative benchmarks" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Auxin flux vein / phyllotactic primordium in Pisum sativum" ;
