<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-50) maps Laws 1-4 to equations, figures and Lean theorems with line loci; `HexCanalizationLattice` (L736-748) and `simulate_growing_lamina_venation` (L950-972) cite Eq. 2-3, the saturation rationale and the Law 4/4b theorems; the Pass 3 scope statement (L663-679) says explicitly what is and is not implemented; the math-KG YAML registers Laws 4 and 4b with lean_locus and code_locus. Deductions: functions named `simulate_2d_lamina_canalization`, `simulate_sachs_wound_bypass` and `simulate_feugier_venation_topologies` still have docstrings that say \"simulate\" although they construct profiles / draw graphs; only the measurement `method` strings were corrected (-8); the solver parameters alpha = 40, beta = 0.2, phi_s = 1.0, mu = 0.001 (L687-701) are the author's choices with a dimensional argument in comments but no mapping to Mitchison's own parameter values (-5); the stage schedule and vein threshold 3 D_0 are uncited heuristics (-3); Law 3 (polar flux conservation) is cited in the docstring but has no dynamical code path (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L243–L254: simulate_2d_lamina_canalization docstring still claims to 'Simulate 2D cellular lamina auxin transport' for an analytic construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L243-L254>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: `HexCanalizationLattice.step` (L808-828) integrates the seed paper's Eq. 2-3 pair (dS = sigma - mu S - sum D (S_i - S_j); dD = alpha |phi|^p/(1 + (|phi|/phi_s)^p) + beta - gamma D) with a semi-implicit S update, wall re-symmetrisation and a documented saturation; `refine_hex_lattice` (L881-913) implements cell division with conductance inheritance; Law 2 drainage now EMERGES (0.67 < 1) instead of being written in; the saturation law is machine-checked in Lean (bounded + monotone). The Sachs incision is solved on the same engine with blocked walls (L1064-1075) and an alpha = 0 control. Deductions: the remediation item asked for polar PIN1 carrier allocation on a growing mesh and the shipped model is facilitated diffusion on a hex lattice (-6); `simulate_2d_lamina_canalization` (L243-335) and the 12-column profiles in `simulate_mitchison_exponent_sweep` (L170-198) are analytic constructions with hard-coded dip ratios 0.3105 / 0.6895 (L195, L295), and the p = 1.4 point uses a special-cased eff_beta = 0.1766 (L158) so the sweep is partly fitted to its own reference (-8); `simulate_sachs_wound_bypass` (L338-414) is a Gaussian centreline plus the constants 0.9852 / 0.0804 (L408-409), still returned and plotted (-4); `simulate_feugier_venation_topologies` (L446-548) solves nothing - V/E/C are typed in (L493, L523) - so Law 3 has no dynamical realisation (-6); the solved growing lamina yields a basal fan of lattice-aligned strands (two stage-1 strands plus parallel secondaries, Panel C of the growing-lamina PNG) rather than a pinnate midrib, and no parameter study shows that the hexagonal anisotropy is not driving it (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L243–L335: simulate_2d_lamina_canalization writes D and S as Gaussian formulas; drainage fraction 0.6895 (L295) is a constant chosen to hit the 0.31 reference - not a solution of the model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L243-L335>",
        "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L446–L548: simulate_feugier_venation_topologies hand-draws two graphs; V_open/E_open (L493) and V_closed/E_closed (L523) are literals, no carrier dynamics are integrated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L446-L548>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — Morphometric validation: 66/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1142-1333) now returns 16 reference-anchored measurements. The 7 Pass 3 ones are computed from solved fields and several of them FAIL their comparison and say so: beta_1 = 0 vs specimen 1843 (L1245-1253), vein density 0.121 vs specimen coverage 0.416 (L1264-1272), strand angle 26.8 +- 14.2 vs 52.9 deg (L1274-1282), S_vein/S_par 0.67 vs the prescribed 0.31 (L1293-1301); nesting 0.79 +- 0.03 vs the qualitative \"all nested\" of Scarpella et al. (L1255-1262); sink balance 0.983 (L1284-1291); solved Sachs intake 0.991 vs NPA 0.609 vs intact 0.988 (L1224-1233). Deductions: the 9 Pass 2 measurements compare prescribed values with the script's own JSON (now labelled PRESCRIBED / GRAPH TEMPLATE at L1212, L1221, L1308, L1317) and still carry Pearson p-values on 5 points (-10); the reference values for nesting (1.0), sink balance (1.0) and beta_1 (0) are qualitative or model-internal rather than measured (-8); the vein-density comparison is apples-to-oranges (vein cells per lamina cell vs a dilated pixel mask, acknowledged in the JSON) (-5); the relative-tortuosity metric (L1235-1243) is a hop count that returns 1.00 despite a 6-cell deflection, so it does not measure what it claims (-6); uncertainties are SDs across 2-3 stages or single-seed, no replicate seeds (-5)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L1205–L1222: Pass 2 drainage ratio and bypass tortuosity retained, now labelled PRESCRIBED, but still counted as measurements against the same JSON they were tuned to <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L1205-L1222>",
        "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L1235–L1243: sachs_dynamic_bypass_relative_tortuosity: hop-count Dijkstra path returns 1.00 for a 6-cell bypass - the metric is insensitive to lateral deflection <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L1235-L1243>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-canalized-vein-to-parenchyma-conc-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-exponent-sweep-winner-share-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-feugier-closed-areole-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-feugier-open-tree-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-growing-lamina-final-betti1-loops>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-growing-lamina-nesting-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-growing-lamina-new-strand-angle-deg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-growing-lamina-sink-balance-stage3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-growing-lamina-vein-density-stage3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-growing-lamina-vein-drainage-ratio-stage3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-linear-p1-winner-flux-share>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-quadratic-p2-winner-flux-share>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-sachs-dynamic-bypass-relative-tortuosity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-sachs-wound-bypass-tortuosity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-sachs-wound-sink-flux-recovery>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-measurement-specimen-secondary-vein-branch-angle-deg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 6.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — MorphoEval overall 70.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py` (overall 70.1/100, down from 92.8 in v2). The remediation added a genuinely solved Mitchison (1980) canalization model on a growing hexagonal cell lattice (three cell-division stages, conductance inheritance, 16 measurements, 12 self-test checks, 3 new Lean 4 theorems) and a solved Sachs incision bypass with an alpha = 0 control. It reproduces the spatiotemporal order of vein formation in the weak sense that 77-81 % of newly canalized cells lie inside pre-existing intercostal panels and that vein order is stage-ordered, but it does NOT close loops (beta_1 = 0, specimen 1843 areoles), its solved network is a basal fan of lattice-aligned strands rather than a pinnate midrib with secondaries, its emergent S_vein/S_par (0.67) disagrees with the value v2 prescribed (0.31), and its strand angles (26.8 +- 14.2 deg) miss the specimen (52.9 deg). Building the solver exposed that the Pass 2 \"simulations\" of lamina drainage, wound bypass and Feugier topologies are analytic profiles, constants and hand-drawn graphs tuned to the script's own reference JSON; these are now labelled PRESCRIBED / GRAPH TEMPLATE in `measure_morphoeval()` but remain in the figure and the measurement set, and the v2 CLI flags are parsed but unused. Rendering is deterministic and SHA-pinned. Overall 70.1/100 (faithfulness 64.3, reproducibility 83.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 62, Morphometric validation 66, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_comparison.png: rendered output of 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py at d58a084, image/png, 1339843 B, 2700×1680 px, artifact_sha256 7e4e81296d44001edb5c233e120b8436c10f86340b35a12fb0d14eb609089381 (sha256 7e4e81296d44001edb5c233e120b8436c10f86340b35a12fb0d14eb609089381), spec_fingerprint c7349d3e4102c9f6306702949c507eeadd9b480c0de0ed099e56fb40eb8cea36. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c7349d3e4102c9f6306702949c507eeadd9b480c0de0ed099e56fb40eb8cea36; artifact_sha256: 7e4e81296d44001edb5c233e120b8436c10f86340b35a12fb0d14eb609089381; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_reference.json=55e0f743ada83918..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/growing_lamina_reference.json=a51f3d788874ecb6..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg=7f67774708f8e952..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/paper_citations.bib=95f1b35cf42a8ae7..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/paper_citations_pass3.bib=b3a22b5ca5439009..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/scout_manifest.json=94a1d6a85fe649c5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-auxin-canalization-leaf-veins-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109: facilitated-diffusion canalization dD_ij/dt = alpha |phi_ij|^p + beta - gamma D_ij with phi_ij = D_ij (S_i - S_j); linear feedback gives diffuse flow, quadratic feedback gives winner-take-all 1-cell strands whose auxin concentration drops below the parenchyma (S_vein < S_par) | Mitchison (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 295:461-471 & Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262: polar auxin transport canalization and C-shaped vascular bypass regeneration around a transverse stem incision | Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375: PIN1 carrier-allocation dynamics, open trees vs closed areoles; Feugier & Iwasa (2006) 243:235-244: canalization alone does not close loops | Scarpella et al. (2006) Genes Dev. 20:1015-1027 & Kang & Dengler (2004) Int. J. Plant Sci. 165:231-242: higher-order veins form progressively inside areoles bounded by lower-order veins; reconstructed_in_script: SOLVED (Pass 3): Mitchison (1980) facilitated-diffusion canalization with soft-saturating feedback alpha |phi|^2/(1+phi^2/phi_s^2) on a hexagonal cell lattice that divides 12x11 -> 24x22 -> 48x44 (75 -> 312 -> 1281 cells) with conductance inheritance; vein cells 7 -> 29 -> 155, nesting of new strands inside pre-existing panels 0.81 / 0.77, S_vein/S_par = 0.67 (emergent), sink intake / production 0.98, beta_1 = 0 at every stage (also 0 with the irreversible-differentiation ablation) | SOLVED (Pass 3): Sachs (1981) transverse incision on a 20x16 hex stem with a pre-established strand: sink intake 0.991 (incised, canalizing) vs 0.609 (alpha = 0 NPA control) vs 0.988 (intact), 6-cell lateral deflection; hop-count path ratio L_wounded/L_intact = 1.00 (metric insensitive to lateral deflection) | PRESCRIBED (Pass 2, retained and now labelled): 2-pathway exponent sweep p in {0.5, 1.0, 1.4, 2.0, 2.5} (the p = 1.4 point uses a special-cased eff_beta = 0.1766), analytic 12-column and 18x14 D/S profiles with hard-coded dip ratios (0.3105 / 0.6895), a Gaussian Sachs bypass centreline with constants 0.9852 / 0.0804, and two hand-drawn Feugier venation graphs (V=16/E=15 -> beta_1 = 0; V=28/E=41 -> beta_1 = 14) | Automated segmentation of the SHA-256-pinned cleared dicot leaf (primary midrib, secondary angle 52.93 +- 2.53 deg, 1843 closed areoles, vein areal coverage 0.416); transfer_boundary: Hexagonal cellular lattice with isotropic 2x refinement stands in for a growing leaf blade; strand orientations are quantised to ~30/60/90 deg so the branch-angle comparison with the specimen (52.9 deg) is lattice-limited | Facilitated diffusion (Mitchison 1980) is solved; polar PIN1 carrier allocation (Mitchison 1981 / Feugier 2005) is only verified algebraically (Law 3) and the hand-drawn graphs are not its output | Reference values 1.38 / 0.985 / 0.08 (Sachs) and the exponent-regime table in the pinned reference JSON are not digitised from any figure; they are carried as qualitative benchmarks; does_not_claim: Loop closure / areole formation or quaternary areole subdivision (beta_1 = 0 in every solved configuration; the specimen has 1843 areoles) | A finite-element or measured growth field; 3D mechanical blade expansion; polar PIN1 dynamics on a growing domain." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:1235-1243 and 1100-1119 — sachs_dynamic_bypass_relative_tortuosity is a hop count that returns 1.00 for a 6-cell deflection. Use Euclidean segment lengths between hex-cell centres along the Dijkstra path and compare against the 1.38 benchmark only after that benchmark is either digitised from Sachs (1981) or dropped.",
        "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:1868-1871 — CLI flags --alpha, --beta, --gamma, --exponent-p are parsed but never used (also true in v2, which credited them). Wire them into the solver (or remove them) and render a parameter sweep (alpha, phi_s, D_diff factor) showing strand count, nesting fraction and vein density per stage, with >= 3 seeds for uncertainty.",
        "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:243-254, 338-357, 446-461 — docstrings of the three prescribed functions still say \"Simulate\"; rename or re-document them as `prescribe_*` / `template_*` so code traceability matches the measurement labels.",
        "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:243-335 and 150-198 — the 18x14 lamina fields and the 12-column profiles are analytic Gaussians with hard-coded dip ratios 0.3105 / 0.6895 (L195, L295) and a special-cased eff_beta = 0.1766 at p = 1.4 (L158). Replace them with the hex solver run at each exponent p (the engine already takes exponent_p) so the bifurcation curve and S_vein/S_par are solved, and drop the fitted constants; reconcile the solved 0.67 with the prescribed 0.31.",
        "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:446-548 — `simulate_feugier_venation_topologies` types in V/E/C (L493, L523) and the measurements feugier_*_betti1_loops (L1303-1318) still count a drawing as a result. Either implement the Feugier et al. (2005) polar carrier-allocation ODEs on the hex engine (the prototype's circulating-vortex failure must be diagnosed: fix the refinement inheritance of polarity as a vector and add auxin degradation inside veins) and derive beta_1 from the solution, or delete the template measurements.",
        "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:720-730 and 1274-1282 — the solved network is a basal fan of lattice-aligned strands (angles 26.8 +- 14.2 deg, hex axes at 30 deg) rather than a pinnate midrib with ~53 deg secondaries. Run the solver on a second lattice (square with diagonals, or random Voronoi cells) and report the lattice sensitivity of the strand angles and of the vein-order map before comparing with the specimen.",
        "remediation needed: 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py:950-1034 — loop closure is absent (beta_1 = 0, specimen 1843 areoles). Implement one published loop mechanism and test it: Feugier & Iwasa (2006) auxin production inside veins with bidirectional flux, or Runions et al. (2005) margin convergence points connecting to two veins; measure nested areole subdivision per stage against the specimen's areole-area distribution (areas already available from segment_leaf_venation_specimen, L620-640).",
        "remediation needed: datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_reference.json:46-115 — the Sachs (1.38 / 0.985 / 0.08) and exponent-regime \"_ref\" values have no figure or table provenance. Digitise the relevant Mitchison (1980) Fig. 1-2 curves (or state that no quantitative benchmark exists) and version the JSON (dataset_id v2) rather than carrying the Pass 1 constants as references." ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.01e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — Parameter expressivity: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the growing-lamina solver exposes real controls that change the solution - `--irreversible` (Law 4b ablation, beta_1 reported for both), `--growth-alpha`, `--growth-phi-s`, `--seed` and `--print-growth` (L1864-1872, L1876-1889) - and the Sachs engine has alpha = 0 (NPA) and incision = False (intact) controls (L1037-1046) whose outputs differ as they should (0.609 / 0.988 / 0.991). Deductions: no parameter sweep is rendered - the dependence of strand count, nesting or density on alpha, phi_s or the differentiation threshold is not shown anywhere (-14); the Pass 2 CLI flags --alpha, --beta, --gamma, --exponent-p (L1868-1871) are parsed and never read by any function (v2 credited them), so the exponent \"sweep\" is fixed to the JSON table (-10); the 5-point exponent sweep is partly fitted (eff_beta special case at L158) so p does not act as a free parameter (-6); the growth schedule (GROWING_LAMINA_STAGES, L703-708) is fixed and not exposed (-4); the ablation is informative (both 0) but is the only morphospace axis actually exercised (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L150–L162: Exponent sweep special-cases p == 1.4 with eff_beta = 0.1766 so the intermediate regime lands on the reference share <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L150-L162>",
        "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L1859–L1889: CLI: --irreversible / --growth-alpha / --growth-phi-s / --print-growth are wired into simulate_growing_lamina_venation (L1884); --alpha/--beta/--gamma/--exponent-p (L1868-1871) are never used <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L1859-L1889>",
        "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L687–L708: GROWING_LAMINA_PARAMS and GROWING_LAMINA_STAGES: all solver parameters in one place but no sweep over them is run or plotted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L687-L708>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-parameter-expressivity-1> ;
    pk1:hasScore 6.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — Reproducibility package: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`--self-test` runs 12 deterministic checks in ~40 s (L1729-1856), including bitwise determinism of all 16 measurements across two calls, wall-symmetry and strand-survival checks across a refinement, the Lean-mirrored saturation bound, and the solved Sachs controls; the default render regenerates all three artifacts in ~31 s; every input is SHA-pinned; seeds are explicit (1980 / 1981 and seed+g per stage). Deductions: no requirements lock file and the environment is recorded only in this audit (-5); without MPLCONFIGDIR matplotlib writes a font cache outside the repository (observed during this run) and the script does not set it (-3); the unused CLI flags (L1868-1871) make the documented invocation misleading (-3); the irreversible ablation doubles the measurement runtime for a result that is identical (0 vs 0) and is not cached (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L1868–L1872: --alpha/--beta/--gamma/--exponent-p parsed but unused; only --seed reaches the solver (via --print-growth) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L1868-L1872>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-repro-package-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

