<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization: exponent bifurcation, growing hex-lamina canalization (solved), Sachs wound bypass (solved + prescribed), hand-drawn Feugier venation templates, and cleared-leaf specimen segmentation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Judged on the regenerated comparison PNG and the new growing-lamina PNG. Panels E/F still show the pinned cleared leaf with the tracked midrib, secondary-angle rays and 1843 segmented areoles, and the solved growing lamina (Panel D of the comparison PNG; A1-A3 and C of the growing-lamina PNG) is now an actual model output placed beside the specimen numbers. Deductions: the solved network has no closed areoles at all (beta_1 = 0 vs 1843 on the specimen) so the defining feature of the specimen's reticulate venation is absent (-15); it is a basal fan of two lattice-aligned strands with parallel secondaries, not the pinnate midrib + ~53 deg secondaries of the specimen (-10); the GIF now shows the solved lamina but the stage-1 and stage-2 frames are too coarse (75 / 312 cells) to resemble a leaf (-4); the comparison PNG still displays the prescribed Pass 2 lamina profiles and bifurcation curve (Panels A-B) as if they were outputs, with no side-by-side against Mitchison's own Fig. 1-2 (-6); Panel F's areole scatter overlays only the first 120 centroids, concentrated at the top margin, so the 1843 count is not visually verifiable (-3); credit for the honest beta_1 / specimen annotation in Panel D and the removal of the hand-drawn Feugier graph from the figure (+5 relative to deleting it silently)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py L720–L730: leaf_blade_hex_mask: analytic ovate outline, not the specimen's outline; no registration of the simulated blade to the specimen <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L720-L730>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-specimen-match-2>,
