<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980) Linear vs Quadratic Flux-Canalization Symmetry Breaking Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why linear feedback (p <= 1) damps conductivity perturbations back to a broad diffuse sheet whereas quadratic feedback (p = 2) triggers supercritical pitchfork winner-take-all symmetry breaking into 1-cell-wide vascular strands | Variables: D_ij: intercellular auxin diffusivity across cell wall (i,j); φ_ij = D_ij(S_i - S_j): auxin flux; p: feedback exponent (p<=1 diffuse sheet, p=2 single-cell strand); α: flux reinforcement gain; β: basal diffusivity synthesis; γ: carrier degradation rate" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207(1166):79-109 Eqs. 2-6 & Fig. 1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L95-L215>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L29-L48> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def linear_canalization_rhs (alpha beta gamma dS D : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * (D * dS) + beta - gamma * D
def quadratic_canalization_rhs (alpha beta gamma dS D : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * (D * dS) * (D * dS) + beta - gamma * D
theorem mitchison_1980_quadratic_vs_linear_symmetry_breaking
    (alpha beta gamma dS D1 D2 : Int) :
    D2 * linear_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D1 -
      D1 * linear_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D2 = beta * (D2 - D1) ∧
    D2 * quadratic_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D1 -
      D1 * quadratic_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D2 =
      (D1 - D2) * (alpha * dS * dS * D1 * D2 - beta)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dD_ij/dt = α |φ_ij|^p + β - γ D_ij;  D_2 dD_1/dt - D_1 dD_2/dt = β(D_2 - D_1) (p=1, diffuse)  vs  (D_1 - D_2)(α (ΔS)^2 D_1 D_2 - β) (p=2, winner-take-all canalization)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.quadratic_canalization_rhs" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.mitchison_1980_quadratic_vs_linear_symmetry_breaking" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980) Canalized Vein Auxin Concentration Drainage Law (S_vein < S_parenchyma)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that quadratic flux-driven conductivity growth drops the auxin concentration inside a canalizing vein below that of surrounding parenchyma (S_vein < S_par), turning the differentiating vein into a lateral drainage sink that recruits tributaries and bypasses stem wounds (Sachs 1981) | Variables: S_vein, S_par: steady-state auxin concentration inside the canalized vascular strand vs surrounding parenchyma; φ_vein, φ_par: axial auxin flux in vein vs parenchyma" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207:79-109 Fig. 2 & pp. 83-87; Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L220-L355>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L66-L78> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def steady_conductivity_scaled (alpha beta phi : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * phi * phi + beta
def drainage_conc_diff_scaled (alpha beta phi_vein phi_par : Int) : Int :=
  phi_par * steady_conductivity_scaled alpha beta phi_vein -
    phi_vein * steady_conductivity_scaled alpha beta phi_par
theorem mitchison_1980_vein_concentration_drainage (alpha beta phi_vein phi_par : Int) :
    drainage_conc_diff_scaled alpha beta phi_vein phi_par =
      (phi_vein - phi_par) * (alpha * phi_vein * phi_par - beta)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "D^*(φ) = (α φ^2 + β)/γ,  S(φ) = φ / D^*(φ)  ⇒  S_par - S_vein = (φ_vein - φ_par)(α φ_vein φ_par - β) / (γ D_vein D_par) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.drainage_conc_diff_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.mitchison_1980_vein_concentration_drainage" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1981) & Feugier et al. (2005) Polar Carrier-Allocated Intercellular Flux Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees exact pairwise intercellular auxin conservation while enabling polar transport against concentration gradients and governing the Feugier et al. (2005) topological transition between open hierarchical venation trees (β_1 = 0) and closed-areole venation loops (β_1 > 0) | Variables: P_ij: directed PIN1 efflux carrier permeability on membrane face i→j; S_i: cytoplasmic auxin concentration in cell i; D_0: apoplastic passive diffusivity; β_1 = E - V + C: venation graph cycle rank (areole loop count)" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 295:461-471 Eqs. 1-5; Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375 Eqs. 1-9 & Figs. 3-7" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L360-L495>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L92-L103> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def polar_canalization_flux (P_ij P_ji D0 S_i S_j : Int) : Int :=
  P_ij * S_i - P_ji * S_j + D0 * (S_i - S_j)
theorem feugier_2005_polar_flux_conservation (P_ij P_ji D0 S_i S_j S : Int) :
    polar_canalization_flux P_ij P_ji D0 S_i S_j +
      polar_canalization_flux P_ji P_ij D0 S_j S_i = 0 ∧
    polar_canalization_flux P_ij P_ji D0 S S = (P_ij - P_ji) * S
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "φ_{i→j} = P_ij S_i - P_ji S_j + D_0(S_i - S_j),  φ_{i→j} + φ_{j→i} = 0;  dP_ij/dt = F(φ_{i→j}, P_cell) - γ P_ij" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.polar_canalization_flux" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.feugier_2005_polar_flux_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980) Saturating Flux-Feedback Canalization on a Growing Lamina — Boundedness & Monotonicity Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees that the flux feedback stays bounded (F ≤ α φ_s^2) as total lamina production grows with cell number, while preserving the Law 1 winner-take-all ordering (more flux => at least as much reinforcement), which is why a hierarchy of strand orders can be solved across three growth stages without a hard conductance cap turning strands into sheets | Variables: φ_ij = D_ij (S_i - S_j): wall flux on the hexagonal cell lattice; φ_s: soft-saturation flux (1.0 = 100 cells' production); α, β, γ as in Law 1; the lamina grows by cell division (4x cells per stage) so the midrib flux grows 4x per stage" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207:79-109 Eqs. 2-3 (feedback form); saturation after Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375 (saturating carrier response)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L732-L1031>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L125-L167> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def saturating_feedback_num (alpha phi phis : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * (phi * phi) * (phis * phis)
def saturating_feedback_den (phi phis : Int) : Int :=
  phis * phis + phi * phi
theorem saturating_canalization_feedback_bounded (alpha phi phis : Int) (h : 0 ≤ alpha) :
    saturating_feedback_num alpha phi phis ≤ alpha * (phis * phis) * saturating_feedback_den phi phis
theorem saturating_canalization_feedback_monotone (phi1 phi2 phis : Int)
    (h0 : 0 ≤ phi1) (h12 : phi1 ≤ phi2) :
    phi1 * phi1 * saturating_feedback_den phi2 phis ≤ phi2 * phi2 * saturating_feedback_den phi1 phis
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dD_ij/dt = α |φ_ij|^2 / (1 + φ_ij^2/φ_s^2) + β - γ D_ij;  α φ^2 φ_s^2 ≤ α φ_s^2 (φ_s^2 + φ^2)  (F(φ) ≤ α φ_s^2);  0 ≤ φ_1 ≤ φ_2 ⇒ φ_1^2 (φ_s^2 + φ_2^2) ≤ φ_2^2 (φ_s^2 + φ_1^2)  (F monotone)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.saturating_feedback_num" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.saturating_canalization_feedback_bounded" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sachs (1981) Irreversible Vascular Differentiation Monotonicity Law (Pass 3 ablation)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises the optional irreversibility rule used as an ablation in the growing-lamina solver; the solver shows that irreversibility alone does not close loops (β_1 = 0 in both variants), carrying loop closure forward as an open remediation item | Variables: d_t: differentiated flag of a cell wall; D_diff = 3 β/γ: differentiation threshold" ;
    dct:source "Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262 (irreversible vascular differentiation); Feugier & Iwasa (2006) J. Theor. Biol. 243:235-244" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L804-L824>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L173-L178> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def differentiation_update (d : Bool) (exceeds : Bool) : Bool :=
  d || exceeds
theorem irreversible_differentiation_monotone (d exceeds : Bool) (h : d = true) :
    differentiation_update d exceeds = true
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d_{t+1} = d_t ∨ [D_ij(t) > D_diff];  d_t = true ⇒ d_{t+1} = true (differentiated wall set is non-decreasing)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.differentiation_update" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.irreversible_differentiation_monotone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980) Linear vs Quadratic Flux-Canalization Symmetry Breaking Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why linear feedback (p <= 1) damps conductivity perturbations back to a broad diffuse sheet whereas quadratic feedback (p = 2) triggers supercritical pitchfork winner-take-all symmetry breaking into 1-cell-wide vascular strands | Variables: D_ij: intercellular auxin diffusivity across cell wall (i,j); φ_ij = D_ij(S_i - S_j): auxin flux; p: feedback exponent (p<=1 diffuse sheet, p=2 single-cell strand); α: flux reinforcement gain; β: basal diffusivity synthesis; γ: carrier degradation rate" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207(1166):79-109 Eqs. 2-6 & Fig. 1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L95-L215>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L29-L48> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def linear_canalization_rhs (alpha beta gamma dS D : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * (D * dS) + beta - gamma * D
def quadratic_canalization_rhs (alpha beta gamma dS D : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * (D * dS) * (D * dS) + beta - gamma * D
theorem mitchison_1980_quadratic_vs_linear_symmetry_breaking
    (alpha beta gamma dS D1 D2 : Int) :
    D2 * linear_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D1 -
      D1 * linear_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D2 = beta * (D2 - D1) ∧
    D2 * quadratic_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D1 -
      D1 * quadratic_canalization_rhs alpha beta gamma dS D2 =
      (D1 - D2) * (alpha * dS * dS * D1 * D2 - beta)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dD_ij/dt = α |φ_ij|^p + β - γ D_ij;  D_2 dD_1/dt - D_1 dD_2/dt = β(D_2 - D_1) (p=1, diffuse)  vs  (D_1 - D_2)(α (ΔS)^2 D_1 D_2 - β) (p=2, winner-take-all canalization)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.quadratic_canalization_rhs" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.mitchison_1980_quadratic_vs_linear_symmetry_breaking" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980) Canalized Vein Auxin Concentration Drainage Law (S_vein < S_parenchyma)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that quadratic flux-driven conductivity growth drops the auxin concentration inside a canalizing vein below that of surrounding parenchyma (S_vein < S_par), turning the differentiating vein into a lateral drainage sink that recruits tributaries and bypasses stem wounds (Sachs 1981) | Variables: S_vein, S_par: steady-state auxin concentration inside the canalized vascular strand vs surrounding parenchyma; φ_vein, φ_par: axial auxin flux in vein vs parenchyma" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207:79-109 Fig. 2 & pp. 83-87; Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L220-L355>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L66-L78> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def steady_conductivity_scaled (alpha beta phi : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * phi * phi + beta
def drainage_conc_diff_scaled (alpha beta phi_vein phi_par : Int) : Int :=
  phi_par * steady_conductivity_scaled alpha beta phi_vein -
    phi_vein * steady_conductivity_scaled alpha beta phi_par
theorem mitchison_1980_vein_concentration_drainage (alpha beta phi_vein phi_par : Int) :
    drainage_conc_diff_scaled alpha beta phi_vein phi_par =
      (phi_vein - phi_par) * (alpha * phi_vein * phi_par - beta)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "D^*(φ) = (α φ^2 + β)/γ,  S(φ) = φ / D^*(φ)  ⇒  S_par - S_vein = (φ_vein - φ_par)(α φ_vein φ_par - β) / (γ D_vein D_par) > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.drainage_conc_diff_scaled" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.mitchison_1980_vein_concentration_drainage" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1981) & Feugier et al. (2005) Polar Carrier-Allocated Intercellular Flux Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees exact pairwise intercellular auxin conservation while enabling polar transport against concentration gradients and governing the Feugier et al. (2005) topological transition between open hierarchical venation trees (β_1 = 0) and closed-areole venation loops (β_1 > 0) | Variables: P_ij: directed PIN1 efflux carrier permeability on membrane face i→j; S_i: cytoplasmic auxin concentration in cell i; D_0: apoplastic passive diffusivity; β_1 = E - V + C: venation graph cycle rank (areole loop count)" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 295:461-471 Eqs. 1-5; Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375 Eqs. 1-9 & Figs. 3-7" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L360-L495>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L92-L103> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def polar_canalization_flux (P_ij P_ji D0 S_i S_j : Int) : Int :=
  P_ij * S_i - P_ji * S_j + D0 * (S_i - S_j)
theorem feugier_2005_polar_flux_conservation (P_ij P_ji D0 S_i S_j S : Int) :
    polar_canalization_flux P_ij P_ji D0 S_i S_j +
      polar_canalization_flux P_ji P_ij D0 S_j S_i = 0 ∧
    polar_canalization_flux P_ij P_ji D0 S S = (P_ij - P_ji) * S
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "φ_{i→j} = P_ij S_i - P_ji S_j + D_0(S_i - S_j),  φ_{i→j} + φ_{j→i} = 0;  dP_ij/dt = F(φ_{i→j}, P_cell) - γ P_ij" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.polar_canalization_flux" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.feugier_2005_polar_flux_conservation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980) Saturating Flux-Feedback Canalization on a Growing Lamina — Boundedness & Monotonicity Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Guarantees that the flux feedback stays bounded (F ≤ α φ_s^2) as total lamina production grows with cell number, while preserving the Law 1 winner-take-all ordering (more flux => at least as much reinforcement), which is why a hierarchy of strand orders can be solved across three growth stages without a hard conductance cap turning strands into sheets | Variables: φ_ij = D_ij (S_i - S_j): wall flux on the hexagonal cell lattice; φ_s: soft-saturation flux (1.0 = 100 cells' production); α, β, γ as in Law 1; the lamina grows by cell division (4x cells per stage) so the midrib flux grows 4x per stage" ;
    dct:source "Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. Lond. B 207:79-109 Eqs. 2-3 (feedback form); saturation after Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375 (saturating carrier response)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L732-L1031>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L125-L167> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def saturating_feedback_num (alpha phi phis : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * (phi * phi) * (phis * phis)
def saturating_feedback_den (phi phis : Int) : Int :=
  phis * phis + phi * phi
theorem saturating_canalization_feedback_bounded (alpha phi phis : Int) (h : 0 ≤ alpha) :
    saturating_feedback_num alpha phi phis ≤ alpha * (phis * phis) * saturating_feedback_den phi phis
theorem saturating_canalization_feedback_monotone (phi1 phi2 phis : Int)
    (h0 : 0 ≤ phi1) (h12 : phi1 ≤ phi2) :
    phi1 * phi1 * saturating_feedback_den phi2 phis ≤ phi2 * phi2 * saturating_feedback_den phi1 phis
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dD_ij/dt = α |φ_ij|^2 / (1 + φ_ij^2/φ_s^2) + β - γ D_ij;  α φ^2 φ_s^2 ≤ α φ_s^2 (φ_s^2 + φ^2)  (F(φ) ≤ α φ_s^2);  0 ≤ φ_1 ≤ φ_2 ⇒ φ_1^2 (φ_s^2 + φ_2^2) ≤ φ_2^2 (φ_s^2 + φ_1^2)  (F monotone)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.saturating_feedback_num" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.saturating_canalization_feedback_bounded" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sachs (1981) Irreversible Vascular Differentiation Monotonicity Law (Pass 3 ablation)" ;
    dct:description "Formalises the optional irreversibility rule used as an ablation in the growing-lamina solver; the solver shows that irreversibility alone does not close loops (β_1 = 0 in both variants), carrying loop closure forward as an open remediation item | Variables: d_t: differentiated flag of a cell wall; D_diff = 3 β/γ: differentiation threshold" ;
    dct:source "Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262 (irreversible vascular differentiation); Feugier & Iwasa (2006) J. Theor. Biol. 243:235-244" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py#L804-L824>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_034_auxin_canalization_leaf_veins.lean#L173-L178> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def differentiation_update (d : Bool) (exceeds : Bool) : Bool :=
  d || exceeds
theorem irreversible_differentiation_monotone (d exceeds : Bool) (h : d = true) :
    differentiation_update d exceeds = true
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d_{t+1} = d_t ∨ [D_ij(t) > D_diff];  d_t = true ⇒ d_{t+1} = true (differentiated wall set is non-decreasing)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2006.05.022>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1086/382794>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.1402406>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/nph.12253>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "With-the-Flux Auxin Canalization & PIN1 Carrier-Allocated Venation Topology" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.differentiation_update" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_034.irreversible_differentiation_monotone" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

